  faqs: [
    { question: "Is there an IB school in Pilibanga or Hanumangarh?", answer: "We could confirm none. A check of Hanumangarh's school listings turned up CBSE and Rajasthan Board schools and no IB World School, and nothing was found in Pilibanga itself. Families who want the IB usually continue a programme begun elsewhere, enrol with a school in Jaipur, Chandigarh or Delhi NCR, or plan a switch at Class 6, 9 or 11. Tutoring is arranged around whichever route applies, and lessons are online wherever the student lives." },
    { question: "Does any school near Pilibanga offer Cambridge or Edexcel IGCSE?", answer: "None that we could confirm in Pilibanga, Hanumangarh or the immediate district. Some families register as private candidates through an approved exam centre, and others look at schools in Jaipur, Chandigarh-Mohali or Ludhiana. A tutor can prepare your child for the exact board, syllabus code and tier whichever route you take, and the choice of centre and series is worth settling early." },
    { question: "Will a tutor come to our house in Pilibanga?", answer: "No. IB Gram tutors do not travel to homes in Pilibanga; in-person home tuition runs only in Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR. In Pilibanga the lessons are private tuition from home, taken live on a laptop with a shared whiteboard and screen-shared past papers. It gives the same one-to-one attention, with the tutor teaching from elsewhere in India while your child sits at a desk in your own house." },
    { question: "How much does IB or IGCSE tuition cost for a student in Pilibanga?", answer: "There is no price list. The rate depends on the programme and level, how scarce the subject is, how long and how often the lessons run and how soon the exam is, and you receive it in writing before booking. Online delivery means no travel, hostel or relocation costs for a Pilibanga family. The first lesson is free and there is no yearly contract." },
    { question: "My child is in Class 10 at a Rajasthan Board or CBSE school. Can we prepare for an IB school in Class 11?", answer: "Yes, and many families do. Preparation is mostly Mathematics, English and the habit of explaining reasoning in writing, which is what an IB school's own admission test usually probes. A tutor can build that foundation and introduce the Diploma subjects at a gentle pace. Admission itself is decided by the school, and neither a tutor nor IB Gram can promise a seat." },
    { question: "Can a student in Pilibanga take the IB Diploma without attending an IB school?", answer: "Not normally. The Diploma is entered through an authorised IB World School that also supervises the Internal Assessments and exams, so a student cannot register from home. That is why Pilibanga enquiries usually come from students enrolled elsewhere or about to move. A tutor supports the subjects; the school remains the route to the examination." },
    { question: "Can my child sit IGCSE exams from Pilibanga as a private candidate?", answer: "Often, through an approved Cambridge or Pearson Edexcel exam centre that accepts external candidates. The centre manages entries and the exam venue, and the availability of subjects and series differs from centre to centre. Science practicals need a plan, usually the written alternative paper at Cambridge. Ask the centre early, because entry deadlines come months before the papers." },
    { question: "Will online lessons cope with summer heat, winter fog and power cuts?", answer: "Largely yes, with some planning. Fog and cold waves disrupt roads and trains, not video lessons, and slots can be moved when conditions are bad. In the hottest weeks we favour early morning or evening times. Because power and connections can fail, keep a charged laptop and a phone hotspot ready, and tell us at the start so the plan allows for it." },
    { question: "Will JEE, NEET or CUET-UG accept my child's IB or IGCSE qualification?", answer: "They can, once equivalence and eligibility conditions are met. The Association of Indian Universities treats the IB Diploma as equivalent to Class 12 and the IGCSE as equivalent to Class 10, and each national exam publishes its own rules on subjects and marks. Read the current notification every year, and choose Class 11 subjects with those rules in mind." },
    { question: "Does IB Gram also run JEE or NEET coaching?", answer: "This service is for IB and IGCSE courses. Entrance-exam preparation is a separate decision, and many IB students handle it alongside their Diploma subjects in their own way. If you are weighing both, tell us the target exams in your brief so the tutoring plan stays realistic about time." },
    { question: "Which IB and IGCSE subjects can tutors cover for Pilibanga students?", answer: "IB and IGCSE tutors in Pilibanga can be matched across the main subjects of both curricula. For the IB: the two Mathematics courses, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management, History, Geography, English, Hindi, Computer Science and Theory of Knowledge. For IGCSE: Mathematics, Additional Mathematics, the sciences, Economics, Geography and Hindi. Send in anything not listed." },
    { question: "Can a tutor help with the IA, Extended Essay or TOK?", answer: "A tutor can help a student choose a workable question, read the criteria, plan data collection and respond to a draft with specific comments. The writing, the data and the final submission remain the student's own, and no IB Gram tutor writes or rewrites graded work. This guidance matters most for students without an IB coordinator nearby." },
    { question: "My child speaks Punjabi or Rajasthani at home. Is that a problem?", answer: "Not at all. IB and IGCSE papers are in English, so lessons run in English, and your child's home language is simply part of the picture. Mention the language mix in your brief and we will keep it in mind when proposing a tutor. Punjabi and Hindi can also be studied as languages within the IB." },
    { question: "When should tutoring start?", answer: "As early as the course allows: Class 11 for the Diploma, Grade 9 for IGCSE, or the start of the MYP years. Early lessons build writing and exam technique before the pressure arrives. A later start still helps if the plan is honest about the remaining time, and a free trial lesson is a sensible way to find out where things stand." },
    { question: "What if the match is wrong?", answer: "Tell us, and we arrange a different tutor. There is no yearly contract, the note after each lesson makes progress visible, and a family can pause or stop at any time. The free trial exists to test the fit before anything is agreed, and a poor match is ours to fix." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram connected to any school, the IB, Cambridge or Pearson?", answer: "No. IB Gram is an independent tutoring service with no affiliation, endorsement or contract with any school or with the International Baccalaureate, Cambridge or Pearson Edexcel. Schools named on this page appear only to show where families from the region might look, and lessons follow the student's own school calendar and the published syllabus." },
  ],

